  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A car of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"m\"></span> travels at a uniform speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span> across a humpback bridge. The bridge is shaped like an arc of a circle with a radius of curvature <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>. Which of the following expressions correctly represents the magnitude of the normal contact force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_N\"></span> exerted by the road on the car at the highest point of the bridge?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_N = mg + \\frac{mv^2}{R}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_N = \\frac{mv^2}{R} - mg\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_N = mg - \\frac{mv^2}{R}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_N = \\frac{mv^2}{R}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
